__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Large, regenerable local artifacts - never commit these. Each one has
# caused an accidental multi-GB commit (rejected by GitHub, since fixed by
# resetting local history) when added via `git add -A`/the GitHub web
# upload UI, which does not respect this file the way `git add` does.
# Regenerate them locally instead of committing them:
#   - checkpoints/                 -> experiments/baseline/filter_training (see docs/reproducibility.md)
#   - corpus_pilot/                -> a local sample of corpus/data/chunks/chunks.jsonl
#   - experiments/results/index_pilot_reduced_scope/ -> experiments/shared/retrieval/build_index.py
#   - experiments/results/index/   -> the full-scale index (~12.5 GB), same command
#   - experiments/baseline/filter_training/.textbook_index_cache/ -> build_labels.py, ~150MB
# Small, legitimate result files (experiments/results/fit_and_evaluate/, the current
# committed run - see docs/evaluation.md SS7) are NOT covered by a blanket
# results/ rule - a real committed result must stay visible to
# `git status`, not silently ignored alongside the large regenerable
# folders sitting next to it.
checkpoints/
experiments/results/index_pilot_reduced_scope/
experiments/results/index/
experiments/baseline/filter_training/.textbook_index_cache/
ram_monitor.csv
experiments/baseline/filter_training/labels/
models/
*.egg-info/
experiments/medchange/data/
